"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 3.8 and an ISUP grade group 2 pathology. Contributing to the risk profile are positive surgical margins, although seminal vesicle invasion was absent and lymphovascular invasion was negative. The absence of nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding nodal status.\n\nInformation that would significantly revise this prognosis includes postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory. A rising or falling pattern in PSA over time is critical for risk stratification. Furthermore, obtaining definitive nodal status through adequate sampling would refine the assessment. Given the positive margins, these findings warrant close monitoring. The current data set provides a limited picture due to missing nodal information. The fixed estimated horizon is 69.39 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 45.11–93.68 months; its coverage has not been validated."
